From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:16:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Compile dxmt_command.metal on the device

The shader library needed Apple's metal/metallib at build time. It is
compiled from source on the device through upstream's winemetal slot 144
(MTLDevice_newLibraryWithSource), with the options Apple's offline
`metal -c` records for it (Metal 3.2, fast math), UTF-8 decoding (the file
is not ASCII) and the remote-mode route. A runtime source compile has no
include path, so the build inlines the file's quoted includes
(dxmt_command_constants.hpp) before embedding it. Without Apple's
toolchain the native macOS airconv and winemetal.so are not configured
(upstream now builds them for aarch64 cross builds too); the iOS unix slice
is built outside meson.

Class: linux-build
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
